# Project 1: MedBridge Health — Company Profile & Security Architecture

## Objective
Develop a fictional healthcare organization's company profile to establish the business, technical, and regulatory context for a Governance, Risk, and Compliance (GRC) assessment.

## Company Overview
MedBridge Health, Inc. is a fictional telehealth organization headquartered in San Francsico, California, providing virtual healthcare services to approximately 40,000 patients.

- **Industry:** Healthcare / Telehealth
- **Employees:** 50
- **Infrastructure:** AWS, Google Workspace, Okta
- **Sensitive Information:** Protected Health Information (PHI), Personally Identifiable Information (PII)
- **Regulatory Considerations:** HIPAA, HITECH, applicable state privacy laws
- **Business Goal:** Obtain a SOC 2 Type II report within 12 months

## Project Scope
- Develop an organizational profile
- Identify critical systems and assets
- Classify sensitive information
- Identify third-party service providers
- Document potential cybersecurity weaknesses
- Develop network architecture and patient data flow diagrams

## Frameworks and Tools
- NIST Cybersecurity Framework (CSF) 2.0
- HIPAA Security Rule
- GitHub
- draw.io (diagrams.net)

## Deliverables
- Company Profile (PDF)
- Asset Inventory
- Network Architecture Diagram
- Patient Data Flow Diagram

## Project Status
In Progress

## Disclaimer
This project uses a fictional healthcare organization for educational and portfolio purposes. All organizational details and security scenarios are simulated!
